OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sun 8 Nov to Tue 17 Nov
OL,6,FHigh pressure is likely to dominate
OL,7,Fconditions across much of the UK
OL,8,Finitially, with large amounts of cloud
OL,9,Fat times but any amounts of rain or
OL,10,Fdrizzle tending to be small. Quite
OL,11,Fbreezy in the south, but a greater
OL,12,Fchance of some fog patches in northern
OL,13,Fareas where winds will be lighter. As
OL,14,Fthe high pressure begins to migrate
OL,15,Faway to the east, frontal systems may
OL,16,Fattempt to bring some occasional rain
OL,17,Fto parts of the southwest and/or
OL,18,Fnorthwest at times, though exactly how
OL,19,Fmuch progress into the UK this makes
OL,20,Fis uncertain. Rainfall is most likely
OL,21,Fto be below average in many areas for
OL,22,Fthis period as a whole, with
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Ftemperatures initially a little below
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Faverage before returning to near or
OL,25,Fslightly above average.
